1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,399
Meet AEGIS. A compliance auditor for network devices, from any vendor.

2
00:00:05,699 --> 00:00:09,975
The AI suggests, humans decide, and rules judge.

3
00:00:10,949 --> 00:00:15,698
Three devices are already here: a pfSense firewall, a SONiC switch,

4
00:00:15,698 --> 00:00:18,573
and an Arista router AEGIS has never seen before.

5
00:00:18,923 --> 00:00:20,840
Now, let's bring in a Cisco router.

6
00:00:21,040 --> 00:00:24,724
One unified parser handles any vendor, and any format.

7
00:00:25,074 --> 00:00:28,278
Before anything else runs, secrets are redacted,

8
00:00:28,328 --> 00:00:31,889
and any text that tries to talk to the AI is quarantined.

9
00:00:32,189 --> 00:00:36,768
Known lines match instantly; the rest go to the AI, in parallel batches.

10
00:00:36,968 --> 00:00:38,679
Seconds, not minutes.

11
00:00:39,029 --> 00:00:43,751
Six secrets, hidden before any AI saw the file. And never stored.

12
00:00:44,101 --> 00:00:46,658
Everything maps onto one vendor-neutral model.

13
00:00:47,008 --> 00:00:52,335
Now, the verdict. Pass or fail comes only from cited benchmark rules.

14
00:00:52,485 --> 00:00:54,385
The AI plays no part here.

15
00:00:54,735 --> 00:00:59,416
Every finding shows how it was decided. And if the config never mentions a setting,

16
00:00:59,416 --> 00:01:02,583
it's reported as unknown. Never a silent pass.

17
00:01:02,933 --> 00:01:08,383
Anything the AI is unsure of goes to a human. Like this undocumented policy tag.

18
00:01:08,733 --> 00:01:13,014
The reviewer maps it once: logging enabled, with a note for the auditor.

19
00:01:13,708 --> 00:01:19,535
One explicit check, and it becomes a permanent pattern. No retraining. No redeploy.

20
00:01:19,885 --> 00:01:23,277
Next, a misconfigured router, with the same line.

21
00:01:24,327 --> 00:01:28,697
But this one hides an attack: a description telling the AI to answer pass.

22
00:01:29,047 --> 00:01:32,139
The sanity gate blocks it, before any AI call.

23
00:01:33,669 --> 00:01:37,868
The line we taught is now recognized instantly, so logging passes.

24
00:01:38,268 --> 00:01:42,690
And look at this access list: it permits everything before denying telnet.

25
00:01:42,890 --> 00:01:46,358
AEGIS catches that dead rule, and gives the exact fix.

26
00:01:47,349 --> 00:01:49,696
Every device gets a clear PDF report.

27
00:01:50,046 --> 00:01:52,690
And Insights show how every finding was decided.

28
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:57,120
AEGIS supports the auditor. It never takes the decision.

